Licence for the files in data/derived/

Everything in this folder is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0), EXCEPT the
two columns named under "Not under CC BY-SA" below.

  Legal code: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode
  Summary:    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The files are DERIVED / MODIFIED from these DoltHub databases, which declare
the same licence (each repo has a LICENSE.md titled "Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International"):

  - https://www.dolthub.com/repositories/post-no-preference/earnings
  - https://www.dolthub.com/repositories/post-no-preference/options

and, for the company names, GICS sectors and CIKs in security.parquet, from
Wikipedia, "List of S&P 500 companies", revision 1382178819 (CC BY-SA 4.0).

Attribution: the original data is from DoltHub, repositories
post-no-preference/earnings and post-no-preference/options, and from
Wikipedia. We selected and filtered it (see the code in src/ and tools/ that
makes each file). We changed the data; DoltHub, Wikipedia and the original
authors do not endorse the changes.

ShareAlike: if you remix or build on these files, you must share your
version under CC BY-SA 4.0 (or a compatible licence) as well.

Not under CC BY-SA (owner decision of 2026-10-29: real values the app and the
docs need may be committed). These two columns are derived from Yahoo Finance
prices and fall under Yahoo's terms of service, not under CC BY-SA:

  - timing_check.parquet, column gap_verdict_yf: the verdict of the Yahoo
    overnight price gap on the timing label in use (supports, contradicts,
    quiet). The app's sample_funnel.json carries a share built from it.
  - security.parquet, column in_universe: which 50 companies the study keeps,
    chosen by a one-time Yahoo market-cap rank (the rank itself is not here).

FRED: no column here is a FRED value. The IVs, variances and moves in
iv_daily.parquet and event_iv.parquet are computed from the DoltHub option
quotes with FRED's DTB3 rate as an input (the discount factor and the carry);
they stay under CC BY-SA as above. DTB3 is public domain; FRED asks for this
citation: Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System (US), 3-Month
Treasury Bill Secondary Market Rate, Discount Basis [DTB3], retrieved from
FRED, Federal Reserve Bank of St. Louis; https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DTB3,
2026-10-29.

Cboe: no Cboe value is in this folder or anywhere else in this repository.
security.parquet's cboe_vx_index only names the Cboe index that exists for a
company (VXAPL and four others); it holds no index value.

The timing labels (events.parquet) are not derived from Yahoo data: they come
from the DoltHub calendar and from company press releases. A Yahoo price gap
only decides which events are looked up or read a second time (data model
§2.1, class F).

The licence of the rest of this repository (the code) is the MIT licence in
the LICENSE file at the root of the repository. It does not apply to this
folder. The root DATA.md says what each source's terms restrict.
